                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I played Cosmic Star Heroine across a CachyOS PC, Steam Deck OLED and a Windows 11 gaming laptop and it ran flawlessly on all three with zero technical issues.\n\nThe game nails the aesthetic it's going for. The 2D visuals are authentic to the Sega CD era, complete with stylish cutscenes and an absolutely amazing soundtrack. The combat system is a highlight, featuring great character variety and plenty of optional side content to explore. It’s also refreshingly paced and doesn't overstay its welcome.\n\nOn the downside, the writing is pretty weak and the story is predictable. While the combat is fun, it loses some strategic depth in the late game and becomes a bit too easy.\n\nOverall, it's a solid RPG that respects your time and looks/sounds fantastic. If you're a fan of classic 16-bit style RPGs, it's worth a play.",
